From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: weizxfree <weizhangxiang2022@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:40:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat(ui): let an embedding page own the AI

When the editor's URL names its host (?host=<origin>) and the page really
is framed by it, the host's assistant replaces the built-in one:
- Docs: every start of the built-in assistant (Ask AI, ribbon presets,
  context menu, F7, Tools menu) is posted to the host with the selection,
  through the one preset setter (host-bridge.ts useHostOwnedAi)
- Sheets: the selection's Ask AI and the ribbon's Translate are posted with
  the worksheet name and range
- Slides: Ask AI on selected elements, and on words selected inside a text
  box (host-text-ask.tsx), ribbon proofing and translate and the context
  menu's AI items are posted with the page, the elements' durable ids and
  the selected words
- the host's chat is the queue: the selection's ask just sends (Enter or
  its one button), monochrome
- no credits notes or prompts; the built-in AI panels stay closed
  (host-ai.css)
- the host can scroll to a block and mark what its agent is working on: the
  blocks in Docs, the range in Sheets (ai-busy-range.ts, a canvas extension)
  and the elements in Slides (host-busy.tsx, a frame over the canvas)
- the editor hands MCP agent commands the same stores the built-in agent gets
